 ```
 
+## Additional frozen backbones: Chronos-2 and Zeus
+
+The same adapter interface also supports two 2026 time-series foundation models:
+
+| `ts_encoder_type` | Source | Representation sent to projector | Width | Context limit | Normalization |
+|---|---|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `chronos2` | [`amazon/chronos-2`](https://huggingface.co/amazon/chronos-2) | encoder context patches, excluding REG/future tokens | 768 | 8,192 | official instance norm + `asinh` inside Chronos-2 |
+| `zeus` | [`GestaltCog/zeus`](https://huggingface.co/GestaltCog/zeus) | center/coarsest U-Net scale (32×) | 768 | 4,096 | valid-point instance norm + `asinh` in this adapter |
+
+Chronos-2 uses 16 points per output token; Zeus begins with point-wise tokenization and the adapter takes its
+32× center-scale representation. Both return ChatTS' original `(flattened_features, patch_cnt)` contract, so the
+processor, datasets, `<ts>` merge logic, and LLM code remain unchanged.
+
+Install Chronos-2 (Python 3.10 or newer):
+
+```bash
+pip install -e ".[chronos2,deepspeed]"
+```
+
+Zeus needs no extra package beyond the base project. This repository includes an audited eager-attention
+implementation with the exact 167 official checkpoint keys/shapes, avoiding the upstream `basicts==1.1.0`
+Transformers pin and unconditional FlashAttention import:
+
+```bash
+pip install -e ".[zeus,deepspeed]"
+```
+
+Select one backbone in stage 1:
+
+```bash
+# Chronos-2
+--ts_encoder_type chronos2 \
+--chronos2_model_name_or_path amazon/chronos-2
+
+# Zeus
+--ts_encoder_type zeus \
+--zeus_model_name_or_path GestaltCog/zeus
+```
+
+Stage 2 should point `model_name_or_path` at the complete stage-1 checkpoint and use
+`--ts_encoder_type auto`; the saved config reconstructs the same backbone and restores its projector.
+Templates are provided in:
+
+- `scripts/full/train_chronos2_stage1.sh` and `scripts/full/train_chronos2_stage2.sh`
+- `scripts/full/train_zeus_stage1.sh` and `scripts/full/train_zeus_stage2.sh`
+
+Do not add another manual z-score step in the shell script: both paths already normalize per series. The external
+backbone is always frozen and excluded from the ChatTS checkpoint. Under DeepSpeed, each rank still holds one
+frozen backbone copy, so budget roughly another 120M parameters for Chronos-2 or 102M for Zeus per rank.
+
+Known Zeus upstream artifact issue: its current Hugging Face config contains both `n_heads=[4,4,8,8,8,4,4]`
+and paper-style `num_heads=[6,12,12,12,6]`, while the released model code reads `n_heads`. The adapter deliberately
+matches the released artifact instead of silently changing its attention partition; confirm this with the Zeus
+authors before treating a paper-head variant as equivalent.
+
 
 ## Steps to reproduce
 1. Download the training datasets from [ChatTS-Training-Dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/ChatTSRepo/ChatTS-Training-Dataset). Put the folders under `data/` (e.g., `data/align_256/`, `data/align_random/`, etc).
